     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the total daily dose looks unsafe.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day** of metformin. That's about twice the maximum labeled dose:\n- Immediate-release metformin: max **2550 mg/day** (for example, 850 mg three times daily)\n- Extended-release metformin: max **2000 mg/day**\n\nDoses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI side effects, even with normal kidney function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **Metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum). This seems the most likely, since 850 \u00d7 2 = 1700.\n2. **Metformin 1700 mg by mouth once daily** with a meal, or split as 850 mg twice daily\n3. **Metformin 1000 mg by mouth twice daily** (2000 mg/day, a common maintenance dose)\n4. Something else, or an extended-release formulation\n\nLet me know the intended dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 5100 mg/day, please confirm that and give a brief clinical reason. I'll put it in the order note so pharmacy can see it when they review."
      }
     ],
